{"content":[{"c":["IMMER (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Priest in the time of David. He became the ancestral head of a house of priests: Pashhur, the priest who had Jeremiah arrested and placed in stocks, was a descendant of Immer (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.20.1","r":"Jer.20.1","rawR":"Jer.20.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.20.1","value":"Jer.20.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 20:1"},"). There were 1,052 priests of the subclan of Immer who returned from the exile (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.12","r":"1Chr.9.12","rawR":"1Chr.9.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.12","value":"1Chr.9.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.37","r":"Ezra.2.37","rawR":"Ezra.2.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.37","value":"Ezra.2.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.40","r":"Neh.7.40","rawR":"Neh.7.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.40","value":"Neh.7.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:40"},"). A descendant of Immer helped rebuild the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.29","r":"Neh.3.29","rawR":"Neh.3.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.29","value":"Neh.3.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:29"},") and 128 priests under Amashsai (also a descendant) helped resettle the city and tend the temple (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.13-14","r":"Neh.11.13-14","rawR":"Neh.11.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.13-14","value":"Neh.11.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:13-14"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ImmerPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 20:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.20.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.20.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.20.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.12","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.12","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.12"},{"anchorT